+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5865+) **Python 2 bare-print cleanup:** converted simple active `print "..."` statements to Python 2.4/3-compatible single-string calls such as `print("msg %s" % value)`, using [`wrap_python2_prints_for_linting.py`](/LLM_Helpers/wrap_python2_prints_for_linting.py) plus manual comma-print cleanup. This keeps Civ4 Python 2.4 compatibility while reducing Ruff/Python 3 parser noise so real issues are easier to see.
 - **Repo-wide blank-line trim (`.py` only):** compacted vertical whitespace for tighter **LLM/grep scanning** (denser context, fewer tokens). Blank-line removal only (comments untouched, unlike the collapse scripts), so it is a pure formatting **no-op** (Python ignores blank lines). Scoped to `.py` for now: they are **not user-facing** so there is no readability/loss concern, and the trim is trivial to apply safely.
 - Convert **single quote to double quote** (e.g. `'BONUS_IRON'` to `"BONUS_IRON"`), which allowed to **detect and fix incorrect fields** and later strengthen them with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)`.
 - **Performance & code cleanup:** Broad Python/XML/C++ optimizations (e.g., removed giant ConfigObj docstring (see [KI#21.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#215---addressed--fixed---removed-the-giant-configobj-docstring-very-inefficiently-in-the-python-code-and-commented-out-most-if-not-all-as-well)); cached hot values via `static const`/hoisting; normalized inconsistent asset names (see for example [KI#18](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#18---very-inconsistent-naming-in-some-assets))), **map-type heaviness caching** (`CvGame::recomputeMapnameHeaviness`) so land/naval checks run once per game (feeds UNITAI tuning) (see [KI#42](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#42---enhancedaddressed-tune-ais-preferred-based-unitai-based-on-war-status-offense-mode-defense-mode-combined-power-ratios-of-ennemies-etc-if-any-other-general-sanity-checks-and-efficiency-city-size-map-type-land-heavy-vs-water-heavy-vs-other-if-any-for-example-general-suicide-or-such-tendencies-etc), **bonus-specific builds/improvements caching** (e.g. `CvUnitAI::getBonusSpecificLandBuilds`), [AI Personality Panel performance optimization notes](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching)), **feature-level caching** (AI Personality Panel), refactor **extremely redundant code** (e.g. `refreshUnitSelection` in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)), cache redundant computation (e.g. **store per turn and player** top cities' values `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`), etc.

